# 7. GLT INSPECTION

## Start GLT

Start GLT is manual.

Record:
- Attempt ID.
- JO ID.
- Terminal ID.
- Start timestamp.
- Published checksheet version.
- Complete checksheet standard snapshot.

Use server time.

## GLT GOOD

Allow GOOD Submit only when:
- Every Mandatory parameter is complete.
- All required evidence is present.
- No parameter is NG.
- Backend validation succeeds.

After Submit:
- Close the GLT attempt as GOOD.
- Record server end timestamp.
- Mark JO `READY_FOR_ALLOCATION`.

## GLT NOT GOOD

Allow NOT GOOD Submit only when:
- Every Mandatory parameter is complete.
- At least one parameter is NG.
- Required NG descriptions/evidence are present.

After Submit:
- Close the attempt as NOT GOOD.
- Generate MRI-A.
- Include every NG parameter.
- Preserve the attempt.
- Block Performance Test allocation.

## GLT Reinspection

Before Start Reinspection:
- One general corrective action remark per MRI-A is mandatory.
- No Supervisor repair-completion approval is required.

At Start Reinspection:
- Create a new attempt.
- Use a blank checksheet.
- Load the latest published applicable checksheet version.
- Do not copy previous measurements.
- Preserve previous results as read-only.

## No GLT Abort

GLT Abort must not exist.

Do not introduce automatic GLT NG, timeout, Pause, or Resume.

Browser closure does not terminate an active GLT attempt.

